  "adaptations": [
    "Decorate dynamic relationship edge values with validated integer targets before sorting, preserving the non-suspending comparator boundary.",
    "Reuse accepted physical ffistorage and entitycolumn ports; use compiler canonical layouts for struct construction and identity allocator bulk copies.",
    "Preserve world publication and snapshot APIs; substitute managed native ID arrays and portable public Buffer operations.",
    "Replace original binary framing with a versioned data-only runtime persistence envelope; resolve component registrations by persisted names, validate target ABI/layout/bounds, and reconstruct owned columns through existing world allocation.",
    "Resolve real asset libraries explicitly and bind their real functions lazily; copy returned bytes into managed storage and release native results.",
    "Keep original three-archetype populate/save/load benchmark; add untimed value/membership/alias/repeat-restore assertions.",
    "Copy all nine original snapshottest functions unchanged and invoke them through a small acceptance wrapper."
  ],
